<p><strong>Total planning allowance:</strong> approximately 6-9 student hours and 2-3 parent/admin hours. Tutor time is separate. A complete first-pass draft is the Friday target; unresolved points must be flagged, not hidden.</p>
<p><strong>Official submission constraints:</strong> deadline 18 September 2026, 12:00 JST (11:00 MYT); English, A4 PDF, computer font at least 10 pt, one file per application document. Form 1 requires at least 100 words per answer and no more than 600 overall. The 5 September HiGA email additionally requires the official forms: do not submit this planning document, or a standalone custom-layout report, as an application form. Use the supplied forms directly to avoid ambiguity.</p>
<p>Official guideline: <a href="https://higa-s.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Admission-Guideline-of-Hiroshima-Global-Academy-General-selection-for-foreign-and-Japanese-students-for-2027-Academic-Year.pdf">https://higa-s.jp/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Admission-Guideline-of-Hiroshima-Global-Academy-General-selection-for-foreign-and-Japanese-students-for-2027-Academic-Year.pdf</a></p>
<p>Official forms index: <a href="https://higa-s.jp/en/senior-high/index/application-process/">https://higa-s.jp/en/senior-high/index/application-process/</a></p>
<p>The uploaded Form 4 instructions require both sections, with at least one Formula Booklet formula used in each. Section 2 is limited to five A4 pages; the form provides a reference page and up to four report pages. Form 5 is limited to eight A4 pages including its reference page. <strong>The approximately 2,300-word target is the tutor's target, not an official HiGA minimum.</strong></p>
